# GitHub Actions CI/CD Rules

## Core Principles

- **Automated Quality Gates**: Implement automated testing, linting, and security scanning
- **Environment Promotion**: Use staging environment for validation before production
- **Infrastructure as Code**: Deploy infrastructure changes through CI/CD pipeline
- **Security First**: Implement secrets management and security scanning

## Workflow Structure

```
.github/
├── workflows/
│   ├── ci.yml              # Continuous Integration
│   ├── cd-staging.yml      # Staging Deployment
│   ├── cd-production.yml   # Production Deployment
│   ├── security.yml        # Security Scanning
│   └── dependency.yml      # Dependency Updates
├── actions/                 # Custom GitHub Actions
└── templates/              # Workflow templates
```

## CI Workflow Rules

- **Trigger on PR**: Run CI on all pull requests and pushes to main branch
- **Matrix Testing**: Test against multiple Node.js versions and environments
- **Caching**: Cache dependencies and build artifacts for faster builds
- **Parallel Jobs**: Run independent jobs in parallel when possible

```yaml
name: CI

on:
  push:
    branches: [main, develop]
  pull_request:
    branches: [main, develop]

env:
  NODE_VERSION: '22'
  NESTJS_VERSION: '10'

jobs:
  test:
    name: Test
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
          strategy:
        matrix:
          node-version: [18, 20, 22]

    steps:
      - name: Checkout code
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Setup Node.js ${{ matrix.node-version }}
        uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: ${{ matrix.node-version }}
          cache: 'npm'

            - name: Install dependencies
        run: pnpm install --frozen-lockfile

      - name: Run linting
        run: pnpm run lint

      - name: Run tests
        run: pnpm run test:ci

      - name: Run type checking
        run: pnpm run type-check

      - name: Upload coverage
        uses: codecov/codecov-action@v3
        with:
          file: ./coverage/lcov.info
```

## Testing Rules

- **Unit Tests**: Run unit tests with coverage reporting
- **Integration Tests**: Test against real AWS services in staging
- **E2E Tests**: Run end-to-end tests for critical user flows
- **Performance Tests**: Monitor test execution time and performance

```yaml
- name: Run unit tests
  run: pnpm run test:unit

- name: Run integration tests
  run: pnpm run test:integration
  env:
    AWS_REGION: us-east-1
    STAGE: test

- name: Run E2E tests
  run: pnpm run test:e2e
  env:
    GRAPHQL_ENDPOINT: ${{ secrets.TEST_GRAPHQL_ENDPOINT }}

- name: Performance test
  run: pnpm run test:performance
  env:
    PERFORMANCE_THRESHOLD: 2000
```

## Code Quality Rules

- **Linting**: Use ESLint with TypeScript and NestJS rules
- **Formatting**: Use Prettier for consistent code formatting
- **Type Checking**: Run TypeScript compiler checks
- **Security Scanning**: Use CodeQL and other security tools

```yaml
      - name: Lint code
        run: pnpm run lint

      - name: Check code formatting
        run: pnpm run format:check

      - name: Type check
        run: pnpm run type-check

- name: Security scan
  uses: github/codeql-action/init@v2
  with:
    languages: javascript

- name: Perform CodeQL Analysis
  uses: github/codeql-action/analyze@v2

- name: Run Snyk security scan
  uses: snyk/actions/node@master
  env:
    SNYK_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.SNYK_TOKEN }}
  with:
    args: --severity-threshold=high
```

## Staging Deployment Rules

- **Auto-deploy**: Deploy to staging on merge to develop branch
- **Environment Validation**: Run smoke tests after deployment
- **Rollback Plan**: Implement automatic rollback on deployment failures
- **Infrastructure Updates**: Deploy infrastructure changes through CI/CD

```yaml
name: Deploy to Staging

on:
  push:
    branches: [develop]

env:
  STAGE: staging
  AWS_REGION: us-east-1

jobs:
  deploy-staging:
    name: Deploy to Staging
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    environment: staging

    steps:
      - name: Checkout code
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Setup Node.js
        uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '22'
          cache: 'npm'

            - name: Install dependencies
        run: pnpm install --frozen-lockfile

      - name: Run tests
        run: pnpm run test:ci

      - name: Build application
        run: pnpm run build

      - name: Configure AWS credentials
        uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@v4
        with:
          aws-access-key-id: ${{ secrets.AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID }}
          aws-secret-access-key: ${{ secrets.AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY }}
          aws-region: ${{ env.AWS_REGION }}

      - name: Deploy to staging
        run: |
          npm run deploy:staging
          echo "Deployment completed successfully"

      - name: Run smoke tests
        run: npm run test:smoke:staging
        env:
          STAGING_URL: ${{ secrets.STAGING_URL }}

      - name: Notify deployment status
        if: always()
        uses: 8398a7/action-slack@v3
        with:
          status: ${{ job.status }}
          channel: '#deployments'
          webhook_url: ${{ secrets.SLACK_WEBHOOK }}
```

## Production Deployment Rules

- **Manual Approval**: Require manual approval for production deployments
- **Staging Validation**: Ensure staging deployment is successful before production
- **Blue-Green Deployment**: Implement zero-downtime deployment strategy
- **Monitoring**: Monitor deployment health and performance

```yaml
name: Deploy to Production

on:
  workflow_run:
    workflows: ['Deploy to Staging']
    types: [completed]
    branches: [develop]

env:
  STAGE: production
  AWS_REGION: us-east-1

jobs:
  deploy-production:
    name: Deploy to Production
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    environment: production
    if: ${{ github.event.workflow_run.conclusion == 'success' }}

    steps:
      - name: Checkout code
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Setup Node.js
        uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '22'
          cache: 'npm'

            - name: Install dependencies
        run: pnpm install --frozen-lockfile

      - name: Build application
        run: pnpm run build:production

      - name: Configure AWS credentials
        uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@v4
        with:
          aws-access-key-id: ${{ secrets.AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID }}
          aws-secret-access-key: ${{ secrets.AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY }}
          aws-region: ${{ env.AWS_REGION }}

      - name: Deploy to production
        run: |
          npm run deploy:production
          echo "Production deployment completed successfully"

      - name: Health check
        run: npm run health:check:production
        env:
          PRODUCTION_URL: ${{ secrets.PRODUCTION_URL }}

      - name: Run production tests
        run: npm run test:production
        env:
          PRODUCTION_URL: ${{ secrets.PRODUCTION_URL }}

      - name: Notify production deployment
        if: success()
        uses: 8398a7/action-slack@v3
        with:
          status: success
          channel: '#deployments'
          webhook_url: ${{ secrets.SLACK_WEBHOOK }}
```

## Security & Compliance Rules

- **Secrets Management**: Use GitHub Secrets for sensitive data
- **Dependency Scanning**: Regularly scan for vulnerable dependencies
- **Container Security**: Scan container images for vulnerabilities
- **Compliance Checks**: Implement compliance and policy checks

```yaml
- name: Check for secrets
  uses: trufflesecurity/trufflehog@main
  with:
    path: .
    base: ${{ github.event.before }}
    head: ${{ github.sha }}

      - name: Run dependency vulnerability scan
        run: pnpm audit --audit-level=high

- name: Check license compliance
  run: npm run license:check

- name: Run OWASP ZAP security scan
  uses: zaproxy/action-full-scan@v0.8.0
  with:
    target: 'https://staging.dualinga.com'
    rules_file_name: '.zap/rules.tsv'
    cmd_options: '-a'
```

## Infrastructure Deployment Rules

- **Serverless Framework**: Deploy infrastructure changes through CI/CD
- **Environment Promotion**: Promote infrastructure changes across environments
- **Rollback Strategy**: Implement infrastructure rollback capabilities
- **Monitoring**: Monitor infrastructure deployment health

```yaml
- name: Deploy infrastructure
  run: |
    npm run deploy:infrastructure:${{ env.STAGE }}

- name: Validate infrastructure
  run: |
    npm run validate:infrastructure:${{ env.STAGE }}

- name: Run infrastructure tests
  run: |
    npm run test:infrastructure:${{ env.STAGE }}
```

## Performance & Monitoring Rules

- **Performance Testing**: Run performance tests after deployment
- **Load Testing**: Test system under load to ensure scalability
- **Monitoring Setup**: Configure monitoring and alerting
- **Metrics Collection**: Collect deployment and performance metrics

```yaml
- name: Performance test
  run: npm run test:performance:${{ env.STAGE }}
  env:
    PERFORMANCE_THRESHOLD: 1000

- name: Load test
  run: npm run test:load:${{ env.STAGE }}
  env:
    LOAD_TEST_USERS: 100
    LOAD_TEST_DURATION: 300

- name: Setup monitoring
  run: npm run setup:monitoring:${{ env.STAGE }}

- name: Configure alerts
  run: npm run configure:alerts:${{ env.STAGE }}
```

## Rollback & Recovery Rules

- **Automatic Rollback**: Implement automatic rollback on deployment failures
- **Health Checks**: Monitor application health during and after deployment
- **Rollback Triggers**: Define clear criteria for rollback decisions
- **Recovery Procedures**: Document and automate recovery procedures

```yaml
- name: Health check with retry
  uses: nick-fields/retry@v2
  with:
    timeout_minutes: 10
    max_attempts: 3
    retry_on: error
    command: npm run health:check:${{ env.STAGE }}

- name: Rollback on failure
  if: failure()
  run: |
    npm run rollback:${{ env.STAGE }}
    echo "Rollback completed due to deployment failure"

- name: Notify rollback
  if: failure()
  uses: 8398a7/action-slack@v3
  with:
    status: failure
    channel: '#deployments'
    webhook_url: ${{ secrets.SLACK_WEBHOOK }}
```

## Documentation & Reporting Rules

- **Deployment Reports**: Generate comprehensive deployment reports
- **Change Logs**: Maintain change logs for all deployments
- **Performance Reports**: Document performance metrics and trends
- **Incident Reports**: Document and analyze deployment incidents

```yaml
- name: Generate deployment report
  run: npm run generate:report:${{ env.STAGE }}

- name: Update changelog
  run: npm run update:changelog

- name: Create performance report
  run: npm run create:performance:report:${{ env.STAGE }}

- name: Archive deployment artifacts
  uses: actions/upload-artifact@v3
  with:
    name: deployment-${{ env.STAGE }}-${{ github.run_number }}
    path: |
      reports/
      logs/
      artifacts/
```

